# Code owners: their approval is the one review the root ruleset requires
# (GOVERNANCE.md, "How root changes"). One approval from any owner listed on
# the matching line satisfies the rule. An author cannot approve their own
# pull request, and the ruleset's last-push rule needs the counting approval
# to come from someone other than whoever pushed last — it does not look
# further back. That an owner does not approve a pull request they pushed
# to, so hardening pushed onto a contributor's branch is approved by another
# owner, is convention, not a ruleset rule. Later
# lines take precedence over earlier ones, so the catch-all stays first; add
# an area line below it when someone takes an area over. Owners need write
# access, or GitHub ignores the entry.
# Syntax: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners

